=\"prf-lede prf-story\">As of Oct 12, the record on Haywood County runs from 1951 to 2025, 75 years. On the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 8 grids, January to February came in under 90% of normal in 34 of those years, the most of any pair. In 2025, November to December came in at 43% of normal and October to November at 64%. In 2026 so far, March to April sits at 44% of normal on the middle of the grids, and grid 19088 had its driest year in 2007 at 63%.</p>"}
